{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is the sum of three consecutive integers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22e83b08c640e6e623c53949c7a56700486b001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 17 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 25 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 21\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Testing_Values.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Testing_Values)\">Solution 1 (Testing Values)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Testing Values)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest number, then the numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fafafcb8dbe78fec70b78cd2a2f4a0222372f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba943173cf5e981d32e9caa2b2a41dd5ef43148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. If the smallest number was any lower, then the sum would then go below all of the answer choices, so it cannot be any lower.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest number, then the numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f106db5d3e48c23969de35e7e73051209b85d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2f9d1df8a9f06b8de94748033a85adcdb3278c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 + 4 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. This goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be the answer.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest number, then the numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/774055f560b65f00f2976674966367dca4327f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/5852379d33a7a0a46dbcef089d74aee7e11534f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 4 + 5 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />. This goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest number, then the numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/13836f492fc8894dc3107d7d4af516e4e01bf830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 5, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/9441967f5eb702c3d2daaf3cecc5b8250e622a4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 5 + 6 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest number, then the numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/a/53a272d8cf604fd76bbfb760c541ee7eb6bc1d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 6, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055ffb22edf0f65f5009693fdcd1d8682b70aa25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 6 + 7 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />. This goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be the answer.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest number, then the numbers would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e134c9d5f24ab21c99fbf590601af252619ffd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 7, 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b9790d1d0ad60fa6a4f62fb734ef8804ae3c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 7 + 8 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Variables.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Variables)\">Solution 2 (Using Variables)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Variables)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the second number of the three consecutive integers. The numbers would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b14192dcab3dd2c88cc2e63d35ce9513fc8ba833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1, x, x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Their sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/4497c6868006fffa6c7845d6ea75c2923e44b112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1 + x + x + 1 = 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, our number must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Of the answer choices, the only one that is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/446084ebbd498d914b0d6e2c94ac36d1018b1938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\"